@page "/contact"

<PageTitle>Contact | It's a Budget</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="How to contact the operator of It's a Budget about support, privacy, deletion, or security." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://budget.clintandtara.com/contact" />
</HeadContent>

<article class="public-page">
    <p class="public-page-kicker">CONTACT</p>
    <h1>Contact It's a Budget</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Support is currently provided directly to approved users of this
        private-hosted service.
    </p>

    <h2>Existing users</h2>
    <p>
        Contact your It's a Budget administrator using the same established
        channel through which your account or invitation was provided. Include
        a short description of the issue and the approximate time it occurred.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy and deletion requests</h2>
    <p>
        State that the request concerns privacy or account deletion and provide
        the username involved. Never send a password, financial-institution
        credential, Plaid token, or full bank-account number.
    </p>

    <h2>Security reports</h2>
    <p>
        State that the message is a private security report. Include the
        affected page, what you observed, and safe reproduction steps. Do not
        include another user's data or continue testing after confirming the
        issue.
    </p>

    <div class="public-callout">
        <strong>Public support address pending</strong>
        <p class="mb-0">
            A branded public support email will be published here before broad
            public registration or institution onboarding.
        </p>
    </div>
</article>
